# Terminal-Based KNIRVROOT Interface Implementation Plan

## Overview

This document outlines a comprehensive plan to migrate from the current Fyne GUI to a fully terminal-based solution using Bubbletea for the KNIRVROOT blockchain explorer and administrative interface. This approach will replace both the Fyne GUI and the alternative GUI (altgui) implementations with a streamlined, efficient terminal interface built entirely in Go using the Bubbletea TUI framework.

**IMPORTANT**: This terminal interface implementation will NOT recreate any commands or functionality that are already defined in the CLI_Tool_Development_Plan.md file. The CLI SDK tool handles wallet management, capability registration, and blockchain interaction commands. This terminal interface focuses on node administration, monitoring, and real-time blockchain operations.

## Goals

1. Remove dependency on Fyne GUI and altgui WebView implementations
2. Create a consistent, role-based terminal interface for all node types (Root, Bootnode, Peer, Client)
3. Implement colorful, intuitive terminal UI using Bubbletea framework
4. Maintain all current functionality while improving usability
5. Simplify codebase by consolidating UI implementations into pure Go
6. Provide cross-platform compatibility (Windows, macOS, Linux)
7. Integrate real-time data engineering architecture for enhanced monitoring and analytics
8. Eliminate external shell dependencies for maximum portability

